IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`
IMPORT `cr2-determination-and-death-benefit`

-- Tests of cr2-determination-and-death-benefit.l4 (regulations 63 and 64). Layer 1.
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the regulations and counting on a calendar before the rules were run.

§ `Tests -- regulations 63 and 64`

§§ `63 -- determining a relationship or a death`

#ASSERT `reg 63(1) — the Minister must use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to determine the question` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(1) — the Minister must use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to determine the question` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 63(2) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish the document to the Minister` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(2) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish the document to the Minister` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(2) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish the document to the Minister` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 63(3) — the Minister may require the original of the document or the copy of the act issued by the competent authority` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(3) — the Minister may require the original of the document or the copy of the act issued by the competent authority` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 63(4) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish other information or evidence respecting their relationship` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(4) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish other information or evidence respecting their relationship` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(4) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish other information or evidence respecting their relationship` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `64(1) -- the amount limb, by the date of death`

-- Arguments: date of death; amount of the death benefit; the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of death.
-- Before 1998: two thirds of 10% of 30,000 is 2,000; less than that qualifies, 2,000 does not.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 1997 12 31) 1999 30000
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 1997 12 31) 2000 30000)
-- 1 January 1998 to 31 December 2018: $2,387, whatever the Maximum Pensionable Earnings were.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) 2386.99 30000
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) 2387 30000)
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 2018 12 31) 2386 99999
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 2018 12 31) 2387 99999)
-- 1 January 1998 with a Maximum of 30,000: the old test (2,000) no longer applies; 2,386 qualifies under the new one.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) 2386 30000
-- From 1 January 2019 the text gives no amount test: the limb gives nothing, however small the benefit.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1) 1 30000)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) 2386 66600)

§§ `64(1) -- when a direction may be given`

-- Arguments: paragraph 71(2)(a) applies; date of death; date the estate applied (or nothing); amount; Maximum Pensionable Earnings.
-- The estate never applied: more than 60 days have passed or will pass.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) NOTHING 5000 60000
-- Death 1 January 2020: 60 days after is 1 March 2020 (2020 is a leap year). Applied on that day: in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1)) 5000 60000)
-- Applied the next day: not within 60 days.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2)) 5000 60000
-- Paragraph 71(2)(a) applies, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 5)) 5000 60000
-- The estate applied in time and the death was in 2010: a benefit under $2,387 qualifies, $2,387 does not.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 6 10)) 2000 46300
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 6 10)) 2387 46300)

§§ `64(1) -- to whom`

-- Arguments: the funeral payer exists; there is a survivor; there is next of kin.
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the payment of the funeral expenses`
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the survivor of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the next of kin of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nobody under regulation 64`

§§ `64(2) and (3) -- no more than the funeral expenses, and the remainder`

-- Arguments: the actual funeral expenses; the amount of the death benefit.
#ASSERT `reg 64(2) — the most that may be paid to the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses` 1800 2500 EQUALS 1800
-- more expenses than the benefit: the benefit is the limit
#ASSERT `reg 64(2) — the most that may be paid to the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses` 3000 2500 EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `reg 64(3) — the remainder of the death benefit that may be directed as if there were no such individual or institution` 1800 2500 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `reg 64(3) — the remainder of the death benefit that may be directed as if there were no such individual or institution` 3000 2500 EQUALS 0
-- Arguments: there is a survivor; there is next of kin.
#ASSERT `reg 64(3) — the payee of the remainder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the survivor of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `reg 64(3) — the payee of the remainder` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the next of kin of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `reg 64(3) — the payee of the remainder` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nobody under regulation 64`
